title: Unlocks and skipping a tour
intro: Show When shows anything only while a flag is set, flags named run. last one run of the game, and a dialogue's Stop action ends a tour partway through.
project: Empty | Unlocks

chapter: A tour | A dialogue as the scene starts
create: Dialogue Box
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Tour
add: Dialogue
set: Dialogue.Start = SceneStart
set: Dialogue.Lines = Welcome to the factory.\n[set run.Contracts] Contracts are open now: up top.\nTake one to get paid.\nMachines come next.\nThen workers to run them.
explain: field:Dialogue.Lines | A tour | The tour starts as the scene does. Its second line sets the flag run.Contracts as it's said.

chapter: Shown once it's unlocked | Show When
deselect
create: Button
rename: Contracts
set: Transform.Position = 0, 3, 0
add: ShowWhen
set: ShowWhen.NeedsFlag = run.Contracts
explain: field:ShowWhen.NeedsFlag | Needs Flag | Show When shows its entity only while its flag is set, and hides it, with everything inside it, otherwise. A hidden button can't be clicked, and its shortcut does nothing.
say: In the Scene view it shows as ever, so it can be laid out. It's only hidden while the game runs.
deselect
create: Button
rename: Contracts Group
set: Transform.Position = -5, 3, 0
add: ShowWhen
set: ShowWhen.NeedsFlag = run.Contracts or run.Work
explain: field:ShowWhen.NeedsFlag | Or | Several flags joined by or: this group's icon shows once any of its tools is unlocked.

chapter: A skip button | Dialogue Stop
deselect
create: Button
rename: Skip Tour
set: Transform.Position = 5, 3, 0
set: Button.Action = Do
pick: Button.Targets = Tour
pick: Button.Do = Stop
pick: Button.Shortcut = K
explain: field:Button.Do | Stop | The dialogue's Stop action ends it at once, even partway through a line, as reaching its end would: the box hides, the game moves again, and its Message and Finished go out.

chapter: Play | Unlock, then skip
play
wait: 1
waitgone: Contracts | 2
say: The tour is on its first line, and Contracts is hidden.
tap: E
waitfor: Contracts | 3
waitfor: Contracts Group | 3
say: The second line set run.Contracts, and the button appears, and so does the group's icon: run.Contracts or run.Work holds.
tap: K
waitgone: Dialogue Box | 3
expectvalue: Tour.Dialogue.IsDone = true
say: K skipped the rest of the tour: the box is gone and the game runs on.
stop

chapter: A new run | run. flags aren't kept
play
wait: 1
waitgone: Contracts | 2
say: A flag whose name starts with run. lasts only while the game runs, so playing again starts with Contracts hidden. A New Game button forgets every flag, too.
stop
